comments.message:
> I don't agree this is a requirement until we have a use case that's actually intended to do this

Configuration for hardware does not magically stop at 2 levels of depth.

That's something you came up with. Device-tree does not have this limitation.
For example

```
&i2c0 {
|       status = "okay";

|       /* Hardware monitor with temperature sensors */
|       nct7802@28 {
|       |       compatible = "nuvoton,nct7802";
|       |       reg = <0x28>;

|       |       #address-cells = <1>;
|       |       #size-cells = <0>;

|       |       channel@0 { /* LTD */
|       |       |       reg = <0>;
|       |       };

|       |       channel@1 { /* RTD1 */
|       |       |       reg = <1>;
|       |       |       sensor-type = "temperature";
|       |       |       temperature-mode = "thermistor";
|       |       };
```

> EM config files are intentionally very flat to simplify this problem

That's just ignoring this issue by pretending it does not exist and flattening any config that's too deep.
